  "feature": "p14-precu-item-level-retirement",
  "status": "ready",
  "scope": "Remove NGE combat-level, channelled-stim player healing, primary-stat, expertise, profession-set, fast-attack, Beast Master, exotic, and later combat-stat authority from retained item transfer, use, effect, attribute, medicine, static and dynamic item modifier writers, reverse engineering, crafting, food, resource-sampling, market-search, weapon-core presentation, dynamic-loot, static-parser consumers, collection rewards, generic player buff effects, stale entitlement reimbursement, and persisted player-stat paths while preserving PRE-CU skill ownership, immediate authored medicine healing, HAM rules, camouflage, authentic Publish-era combat haste and slow, NPC/quest buff compatibility, and retained expansion content.",
  "eraEvidence": {
    "userRule": "PRE-CU has no player combat-level stat; retained content must not require one.",
    "core3Repository": "swgemu/Core3",
    "core3Commit": "6ea64f60ef33b89121c2a8d188b93f4bc6f158e8",
    "surveyReference": "SurveySessionImplementation.cpp and ResourceSpawner.cpp derive sampling Action cost from current Quickness as 124 - Quickness / 12.5 and never consult player combat level.",
    "dynamicLootReference": "Publish-era skills authenticate camouflage as a PRE-CU Bothan and Ranger skill modifier; precision_modified, strength_modified, stamina_modified, constitution_modified, agility_modified, and luck_modified are later primary-stat vocabulary and are not PRE-CU dynamic-loot authority.",
    "staticConsumableReference": "Combat level is not a PRE-CU player/item admission stat. Retained expansion healing content keeps authored healing power, action-pool selection, charges, no-trade state, scripts, templates, and weapon-core quality lookup while combat-level objvars and UI/search presentation are retired.",
    "channelHealReference": "The pinned Publish 14.1 Core3 tree contains no channel_heal effect, channel_healing buff, useChannelHealItem path, five delayed healing ticks, Luck-amplified medicine pulse, or medicine countdown UI. The three retained Post Combat Balance channelled-stim templates remain expansion content, but player use now adapts to the existing immediate authored medicine-heal path; stale player buff, callback, script-var, and owned countdown state fail closed while non-player compatibility remains available.",
    "staticSkillModifierReference": "The pinned Publish 14.1 Core3 tree contains no NGE expertise system, six-stat primary-modifier vocabulary, fast_attack_line_, Beast Master incubation, later block/strikethrough, Dire, Officer cooldown/rally, or tka_armor authority. Retained static armor, weapons, jewelry, and items remain available, while their common initializer filters those NGE modifier families. Authentic PRE-CU droid_find_speed plus poison/disease/fire/bleeding resistance and absorption remain applied; Publish 14.1 Core3 uses unarmed_toughness rather than the NGE expertise listing's Innate Teras Kasi Armor.",
    "itemWriterReference": "The retained reverse-engineering, magic-item, buff-effect, and collection-reward tables mix authentic PRE-CU crafting, healing, camouflage, droid, resistance, absorption, combat_haste, and combat_slow modifiers with later NGE expertise, six-primary-stat, Beast Master, exotic, evasion, strikethrough, damage-multiplier, attack-avoidance, and combat-rating vocabulary. Common runtime classification now filters later-only modifiers at generation, parsing, crafting, consumable, equip, transfer, player buff, collection reward, stale reimbursement, and login-cleanup ingress while retaining expansion data and NPC/quest compatibility; the six always-generated reverse-engineering slots use authenticated PRE-CU assembly modifiers."
  },
